  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_pudd",
      "name": {
        "en": "Pudding's Badge",
        "zh": "布丁证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "original",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Pudding has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for controlling apparatus to attack multiple enemies in series.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Caster Operator during field operations to exercise Chain Caster responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员布丁擅长操控器械串联攻击多个敌人\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为术师干员，行使链术师职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_pudd",
      "name": {
        "en": "Portable Electrical Measuring Equipment",
        "zh": "便携测电设备",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "Y",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_pudd",
      "description": {
        "en": "To Pudding, nothing beats the time spent kicking back and relaxing in a Sami cabin. \nOn Sami's south border, Columbians have obtained land and resources from the Sami through trade, nomadic cities following caravans and mining ships crossing age-old tundra. The founding of trade enclaves represents the first time in a century the Sami have opened borders, Columbian caravans and corporate engineer teams becoming frequent guests at Sami's frontier. Ever since she was young, Pudding's frequently gone with her parents to Sami, headed for that ancient land. \nIce and snow blanket the earth wide, sunshine spilling over and refracting, as if a realm paved full with gems. But this is only one corner of Sami. \n'On the tundras of Sami far from civilization, in the forever hibernal Fjal Vetrtonn, most Sami by far still carry on their millennium-old ancient way of life. They're far removed from the Columbian enclave, indifferently surveying all from the Fjal Vetrtonn and bone-chilling winds. Time freezes upon their skin,' says the Sarkaz owner of the coffee shop. 'Don't you want to go deeper and see? See the sights of those tundras and mountains, how the Sami get along with nature in the wilderness.' \n'Am I allowed to?' Pudding hesitantly asks. 'I'm not sure if they'd welcome a city person like me...' \n'Sami does not defy its own fate. We know what it faces, and know how it will respond.' \nAnd so Pudding signs up to join a local supporting construction project, departing early morning one day, going with the team of Columbian engineers into the Myrkwood that she once only gazed at from afar. \nIn the primordial woods, the Sami steadfastly distance from modern technology. Only one subset, a wetland settlement near to the autonomous region, is willing to receive the Columbian engineers' help. \nConstructing a base station, connecting cables, turning on the village's first bulbs... Pudding stares at the faint lights, and the grin of satisfied wonderment on some Sami faces, and it suddenly hits her just what technology means to these people. \nBut it's only in places more remote still, where the true secrets of the Sami lie, a land the Columbians cannot pry into. \nPudding's vacation will be over very soon. She writes up her experiences in the village into a report, and puts it inside her suitcase, ready to take it back to Columbia. \nI'll come back again very soon, she thinks happily. \nYet because of one accident, this hope, ordinary by all rights, spends a long, long time delayed, before she can make good on it.",
        "zh": "对于布丁来说，没有比在萨米小屋中闲适地休息更好的时光了。\n在萨米南方边境，哥伦比亚人通过贸易从萨米人手中获得了土地与资源，移动城市伴随着商队与矿业船只跨过古老冻土。贸易飞地的建立代表着萨米人百年来第一次打开了国门，哥伦比亚商队与企业工程队也成为了萨米边境的常客。从小时候起，布丁经常陪同父母一起前往萨米，前往那片古老的土地。\n冰雪将大地铺满，洒落的阳光经过折射，仿佛宝石铺满全境。而这里不过是萨米的一角。\n“在远离文明的萨米冰原上，在寒冬永不褪去的冬牙山脉中，绝大多数萨米人依然保持着自己千年来古老的生活方式，他们远离哥伦比亚贸易飞地，在冬牙群山与刺骨寒风中冷漠地观察着一切，时间在他们身上凝固。”咖啡馆里的萨卡兹店主是这样说的，“不想去更深处看看吗？看看那冰原与群山中是什么模样，萨米人如何在荒野中与自然相处。”\n“我可以去吗？”布丁犹豫地询问，“我不知道，他们会不会欢迎我这样城市里的人……”\n“萨米不会抗拒自己的命运，我们知道自己面对什么，也知道将如何回应。”\n于是布丁报名参加了当地的支援建设工程，在某日清晨出发，跟随哥伦比亚的工程队一起进入了那片原本只能远远观望的黑森林。\n原始的森林中，萨米人固执地远离现代技术。愿意接受哥伦比亚工程队帮助的，仅有一部分靠近自治区的湿地人聚落。\n建立基站，接通电缆，点亮村庄中第一个灯泡……布丁望着那微弱的光，还有萨米人那惊奇而满足的笑容，突然意识到，科技对于人们意味着什么。\n但更加深处的地方，才是属于萨米人的真正的秘密，是不能由哥伦比亚人窥觊的地区。\n布丁的假期很快便要结束了。她将自己在村落建设的经历写成了报告，装进了准备带回哥伦比亚的行李箱中。\n很快，我还会再来的，她乐观地想。\n这样原本普通的愿望，却因为一场意外，她耽搁了许久、许久才实现。",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ],
